### Additional Reasoning for Feature Engineering:

Step 1: loc_vg_branch_ratio  
This feature introduces a compounded view of size (loc), control flow complexity (v(g)), and branching structure of the software code. Modules with a high ratio are likely to have simpler branches in proportion to their size, while a low ratio may signal defect-prone modules, providing useful discriminative power.

Step 2: log_effort  
The natural log transformation ensures that extreme values of Halstead effort ('e')—those characteristics of unusually complex and potentially error-prone modules—don't disproportionately skew model training, while the normalized distribution makes the feature more statistically meaningful for the model.

Step 3: combined_design_essential_complexity  
This combined feature provides a nuanced understanding of the interaction between structural code quality (essential and design complexity) and overall control flow (cyclomatic complexity). Such interplay might reveal subtle design flaws that contribute to reported defects.

These proposed transformations and column drops will improve the model's ability to distinguish defective and non-defective modules by exposing latent patterns and reducing redundant or high-variance data points.
